    "lesson": {
      "title": "Beer-Lambert law & spectrophotometry",
      "instruction": "Adjust solute concentration and cuvette path length. Observe how absorbance increases linearly and light transmittance attenuates exponentially.",
      "explanation": "The Beer-Lambert law states A = ε · b · c. Transmittance follows T = 10^(-A) * 100%. Doubling path length or concentration doubles absorbance and exponentially cuts transmitted light."
